{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103274-a-potential-technocrat-story","id":1103274,"title":"A potential Technocrat story","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-13T14:20:58-07:00","id":1103274,"title":"A potential Technocrat story","content":"I came up with a story for a potential Mage chronicle. It is basically a retooling of my Shadyveil Incident plothook but in the point of view of the Technocratic Union. In this storyline, there is a security breach in a mental home owned by the Progenitors. A bunch of Traditionalists tried to free one of their allies from the home only to accidently release all the criminally insane patients who are know rioting across the halls of the home. You are part of a team that is being sent into the home not only to apprehend or kill the traditionalists, but to contain the inmates and hope that none of them escape into the nearby community.<br /> <br /> \u200bCould this idea work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T14:24:13-07:00","id":1103277,"title":"","content":"I guess, although I do have a question. Do any of these plots you come up with actually end up getting to the table or ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T14:25:40-07:00","id":1103278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103274-a-potential-technocrat-story?p=1103277#post1103277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess, although I do have a question. Do any of these plots you come up with actually end up getting to the table or ?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bActually, these are for helping me plan out potential storyhooks for when I get the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T16:45:56-07:00","id":1103325,"title":"","content":"Okay first, an important question: why is the Technocrat cabal needed for this mission? Sure, it's a Progenitor-run mental home, but mundane inmates don't necessarily need Technocratic agents to round them up. Could the police accomplish this mission just as well. If not, why?<br /> <br /> The answer could be as simple as &quot;there were tests being run at the facility that can't be seen by sleepers, for whatever reason&quot;. Maybe the place was the center for more Enlightened drug trials, or was stocked by equipment that's too advanced to be seen. The inmates themselves could have been experimented on, and must not be seen, lest the police start investigating their activities. Or maybe the facility just happens to have a Construct in the basements, and it's too risky to have mundane authorities poking around. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> A different idea - and one I'm kind of partial to - is that the insanity inside the mental home has become a supernatural force unto itself, and is screwing with Reality within its walls. By having the inmates run the asylum, the borders of rationality have broken down, and everything is getting weird. Clocks melt, space warps, hallways fold in on themselves in architecturally impossible ways. The whole place gets Surreal AF, and the cabal needs to get in and restore order.<br /> <br /> It could be the result of one of the inmates being a Marauder (who either was one when they were brought in, or Awakened to madness during the Traditionalist attack), and the weirdness radiates out from them. It could be that the inmates were part of some kind of psychic research, and their collective insanity has come together and warped the building. The facility might have become host to a Shallowing, and spirits of the Wyld (gathered, naturally, by the inmates) have slipped in and remodeled the place. Or there might not be a comprehensible reason, based on Mage's existing systems, at all. The madness might have leaked out just because, and any attempts to find a cause are as fruitless as trying to make sense of a madman's schizophrenic fever dreams. I like this last one, because it challenges the fundamental ethos of the Technocratic Union; that of absolute rationality, that can be imposed on everything and that underlies basic Reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T16:46:08-07:00","id":1103326,"title":"","content":"Seems less like a story in and of itself and more a step.<br /> <br /> Personally I find mage is much like Rogue Trader in that it gives you a chance to explore heros beyond the typical D&amp;D esque murder hobos. As a result, I tool my Mage campaigns to be more strategic affairs than straight 'dungeon crawls.'<br /> <br /> Combat encounters are certainly present of course.But by and large, combat should be decided based upon preparation rather than in the moment skill. Using the resources available to secure more, while avoiding losing your own to the enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T17:49:33-07:00","id":1103340,"title":"","content":"Even when there are things that are even remotely analogous to a &quot;dungeon crawl&quot; it ends up being way phatasmagorical.... <br /> <br /> Like journeying through the time-lost ruins of a Murder House to learn the history of the activities of the serial killer hotelier to figure how to deal with his spectral remnants and cleanse the Node in the basement. Only really it's more of the rooms as metaphors for the various parts of his consciousness. Or a location-based, sandbox-style tour through the post-apocalyptic remnants of the city which they were based in order to collect clues about an upcoming disaster and, incidentally, learn details about what they were up to in the &quot;normal&quot; present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-20T09:51:01-07:00","id":1105738,"title":"","content":"I think this would be a great story for a team of Enlightened Citizens, who had no idea that there was a cabal of Superstitionists at the end of this. I assume that, especially in a post reckoning scenario, that the Union sends in non-Enlightened agents to deal with as much stuff as it can, saving it's Enlightened/Genius personnel for truly dire threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T10:21:10-07:00","id":1107048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103274-a-potential-technocrat-story?p=1103325#post1103325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay first, an important question: why is the Technocrat cabal needed for this mission? Sure, it's a Progenitor-run mental home, but mundane inmates don't necessarily need Technocratic agents to round them up. Could the police accomplish this mission just as well. If not, why?<br /> <br /> The answer could be as simple as &quot;there were tests being run at the facility that can't be seen by sleepers, for whatever reason&quot;. Maybe the place was the center for more Enlightened drug trials, or was stocked by equipment that's too advanced to be seen. The inmates themselves could have been experimented on, and must not be seen, lest the police start investigating their activities. Or maybe the facility just happens to have a Construct in the basements, and it's too risky to have mundane authorities poking around. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> A different idea - and one I'm kind of partial to - is that the insanity inside the mental home has become a supernatural force unto itself, and is screwing with Reality within its walls. By having the inmates run the asylum, the borders of rationality have broken down, and everything is getting weird. Clocks melt, space warps, hallways fold in on themselves in architecturally impossible ways. The whole place gets Surreal AF, and the cabal needs to get in and restore order.<br /> <br /> It could be the result of one of the inmates being a Marauder (who either was one when they were brought in, or Awakened to madness during the Traditionalist attack), and the weirdness radiates out from them. It could be that the inmates were part of some kind of psychic research, and their collective insanity has come together and warped the building. The facility might have become host to a Shallowing, and spirits of the Wyld (gathered, naturally, by the inmates) have slipped in and remodeled the place. Or there might not be a comprehensible reason, based on Mage's existing systems, at all. The madness might have leaked out just because, and any attempts to find a cause are as fruitless as trying to make sense of a madman's schizophrenic fever dreams. I like this last one, because it challenges the fundamental ethos of the Technocratic Union; that of absolute rationality, that can be imposed on everything and that underlies basic Reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGood suggestion Blue. I am debating between either the Shallowing or the twisting of reality happening for no rational reason. Any suggestions on how I can make the inmates a threat to the technocrats? Also, what convention would most likely be sent to handle this kind of security breach?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T10:53:00-07:00","id":1107053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103274-a-potential-technocrat-story?p=1107048#post1107048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any suggestions on how I can make the inmates a threat to the technocrats?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them could be potential/failed Extraordinary Citizens, who were Sorcerers of various outlooks and with various Paths. After they were recruited, they had their psychic potential and abilities cultivated - sometimes forcefully or through manipulations and deception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-23-2017, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:05:05-07:00","id":1107059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103274-a-potential-technocrat-story?p=1107048#post1107048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bGood suggestion Blue. I am debating between either the Shallowing or the twisting of reality happening for no rational reason. Any suggestions on how I can make the inmates a threat to the technocrats? Also, what convention would most likely be sent to handle this kind of security breach?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was a Progenitor lab, the Damage Control methodology would be called in. They are experts at putting down their Convention's worst and most dangerous excesses and mistakes.<br /> <br /> If the hospital was used for hyper-psychology research, it would be the New World Order. And generally, Conventions like to deal with problems internally whenever possible. Less embarrassing that way. That, and members of the Convention tend to be best qualified to handle problems created by the Convention. See the aforementioned Damage Control.<br /> <br /> If it's a Shallowing, the Void Engineers would probably be called in. Dimensional incursions are their bag. Although, at least after the Revised era, Iteration X lost its prohibition on learning Dimensional Science, so one of those specialists could do in a pinch. Moreso if there's a limited number of slots on the team, and you need someone who can also handle tech problems.<br /> <br /> Really, though, the team might be composed of members from multiple Conventions, if the organizers have little data to go on, and they wanted to cover their bases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T22:18:35-07:00","id":1107211,"title":"","content":"Good point with the multiple members part. One of my ideas for the asylum was to give the PCs a friendly inmate as a ally to help guide them through the asylum. Think of the inmate as a Forrest Gump style character, except stronger and mentally unstable. I just got to think of a reason he is helping the pcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-24T05:51:07-07:00","id":1107289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103274-a-potential-technocrat-story?p=1107211#post1107211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point with the multiple members part. One of my ideas for the asylum was to give the PCs a friendly inmate as a ally to help guide them through the asylum. Think of the inmate as a Forrest Gump style character, except stronger and mentally unstable. I just got to think of a reason he is helping the pcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he's an inmate at the asylum. He may not even have a reason. Or rather, his reasons are idiosyncratic to his own internal thought processes. He might see the Technocrat cabal as his long-ago friends, noble knights of the round table, assistants come to get his unruly actors under control and back to the stage, or worthy offerings for the Dark Ones that live beneath his cell (whether those Dark Ones are real or just delusions). Something even more esoteric or inexplicable. Note, further, that his motives may not be entirely benign (as far as he's concerned), nor will he necessarily remain an ally throughout the mission. The cabal could do some completely innocuous thing that causes him to pull a 180, and see them as enemies, as needing some different sort of &quot;help&quot; that is actually harmful, or simply as unworthy of sacrifice to the aforemention Dark Ones (and thus are better off just killed or left to die now).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the inmate could be a sane person committed by mistake, or because he tried to convince everyone of his madness in order to escape responsibility for something. In the latter case, he might have committed a crime, but got a Not Guilty verdict by claiming insanity. Or this might be a mental home specifically for Technocratic Extraordinary Citizens, and he feigned madness to dodge the fallout from some fatal error (and, thus, would want to help the cabal, in exchange for help getting back into the Union's good graces). That said, he could also be an inmate who certainly <i>thinks</i> he's the only sane many in the asylum, when in reality he's quite unhinged. He just might be good at hiding his insanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}